# Build-context excludes for the root Dockerfile.
#
# This is a plain, classic root-level .dockerignore: the build context is the
# repository root (this directory), and the Dockerfile sits at the root of it,
# so Docker finds this file by its ordinary rules - no BuildKit per-Dockerfile
# sidecar convention involved. It applies to every build from this context,
# including `docker compose build` (ops/docker-compose.yml sets
# `context: ..` + `dockerfile: Dockerfile`) and Coolify, which builds from
# the repository root and offers no way to point at a Dockerfile elsewhere.
#
# DO NOT add any pattern here that excludes `server/` or its subpaths. The
# Dockerfile COPYs from server/ (package.json, package-lock.json,
# server/packages/*, and the full server/. tree in the build stage) - doing
# so would silently produce an empty or broken image with no clear error.

# Version control and repo metadata - not needed inside the image.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Docs and non-server top-level content - irrelevant to the Node build.
README.md
docs
firmware
ops
data

# Local build artifacts / dependency caches on the host. These are always
# regenerated inside the image by `npm ci` / `npm run build`, so shipping
# host copies would only bloat the build context and risk stale artifacts
# leaking into a stage that expects a clean install.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/ui-dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/coverage

# Editor / OS cruft.
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
